<title>TAIWAN: Mitac says buys Merisel unit.</title>
<headline>Mitac says buys Merisel unit.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. unit of Taiwan's computer maker Mitac International Corp has agreed to acquire majority shares of a subsidiary of U.S. computer distributor Merisel Inc, a company statement said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Mitac, through its U.S. unit Synnex Information Technologies Inc, would acquire Computerland Franchise and Datago Aggregation Business run by Merisel FAB, the statement said.</p>
<p>The two sides agreed not to reveal the value of the merger, which will be completed within 30 to 45 days, the statement said.</p>
